RG DS OS: the status and charging LEDs keep their state through sleep

The LED core switches every LED off at suspend unless its node says otherwise. The red status LED is the sleep
indicator (/usr/libexec/rgds/power lights it dimly around the suspend), and the amber one may show charging while
asleep later; both PWMs sit in the PMU's domain. The green power LED still goes out, which is how "asleep" reads.

--- a/rk3568-anbernic-rg-ds.dts	2026-10-27 15:00:00
+++ b/rk3568-anbernic-rg-ds.dts	2026-10-27 15:00:00
@@ -275,6 +275,7 @@
 			function = LED_FUNCTION_CHARGING;
 			max-brightness = <255>;
 			pwms = <&pwm6 0 25000 0>;
+			retain-state-suspended;
 		};
 
 		red_led: led-2 {
@@ -283,6 +284,7 @@
 			function = LED_FUNCTION_STATUS;
 			max-brightness = <255>;
 			pwms = <&pwm7 0 25000 0>;
+			retain-state-suspended;
 		};
 	};
 
